What are Vacuum Thin Films?
Vacuum Thin Films are ultra-thin material layers (typically ranging from nanometers to microns in thickness) deposited on substrate surfaces using physical or chemical vapor deposition techniques under vacuum conditions. These precision-engineered films enhance specific functional properties like optical transparency, electrical conductivity, mechanical durability, or barrier resistance. The technology's ability to control material composition at microscopic levels makes it indispensable across high-tech industries spanning semiconductors, photovoltaics, and medical devices.
